When logging errors that will be thrown, it's better practice to create the Error object first and pass it to both the logger and throw statement. This ensures the error logged has the same stack trace as the thrown error.

Consider:
```typescript
const error = new Error(`[ObjectQL] Datasource '${datasourceName}' configured for object '${objectName}' is not registered.`);
this.logger.error('Datasource not found for object', error, { 
  objectName, 
  datasourceName,
  availableDrivers: Array.from(this.drivers.keys())
});
throw error;
```

The same pattern occurs at line 240.
```suggestion
