When logging HTTP errors, it's better to create an actual Error object rather than passing `undefined` as the error parameter. This would provide better error tracking and stack traces.

Consider:
```typescript
this.logger.error('HTTP request failed', 
  new Error(`Request failed: ${res.status} ${JSON.stringify(errorBody)}`), 
  { 
    method: options.method || 'GET',
    url,
    status: res.status,
    error: errorBody
  }
);
```
